# The right angle test in the matcher is written with || where && was meant.
#
# align_patches.cpp keeps three minima and, when they are not collinear, asks whether they form a
# right angle with minCount at the corner. The first clause is that test: the corner shares a row
# with one of the other two and a column with the other. The second clause is meant to be its
# mirror, and a mirror needs the same &&; written with || it accepts any point sharing a row, or
# any point sharing a column, which is not a corner. The projection that follows divides by
# QUADMESH_SIZE squared, which assumes the two legs have length QUADMESH_SIZE and are orthogonal,
# so on a triple that is not a corner the match is placed wrong by up to a cell, four voxels.
#
# MEASURED, and it is what puts this patch in corrections and not in the inert group. Box w035 of
# PHerc. 0139, seed 3455,2753,5383, 2858 seeds, the whole chain g c l vm hm fm, the reference run
# out0139w035 against the corrected run out0139w035-gfix:
#
#   the test changes its answer         1,482,950 of 7,188,850 tests, 20.63 per cent
#   patches grown                       1,495  ->  1,539
#   patches dropped by stage c            348  ->    329, 23.28 % -> 21.38 % of those grown
#   flattened sheet, ten components     20.4272 cm2 -> 24.5790 cm2, plus 20.3 per cent
#     (area by triangulation in the box, tools/clip_box_tifxyz.py, the same formula both sides)
#   sheet contrast against the CT, all twenty components, weighted by area
#     (tools/contrasto_foglio.py)       blocks resting on a sheet 58.4 % -> 57.4 %
#                                       attached area 11.93 cm2 -> 14.10 cm2, plus 18.2 per cent
#   cover of the published w035 mesh    95.83 % -> 96.27 %, cells within 3 voxels 15.76 % -> 16.20 %
#     (tools/ancoraggio_superficie.py, cubic cells of 8 voxels)
#
# So what the repair buys is a fifth more sheet at the same seating quality, not a better seated
# sheet: the fraction of blocks resting on papyrus does not move. The number quoted on the largest
# component alone, 35.0 % -> 58.2 %, is the choice of that component and not a property of the
# chain, and it is written here so that nobody quotes it later.
#
# The two corrections of this file were run together; the other one is measured identical by
# sha256 on its own, so every number above belongs to this one.
#
# Evidence: runs/rev1/audit/STEVENS-VALLE.md, runs/catena/superficie-stevens/out0139w035-gfix.
